<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  folio-assistant — Ingestion subprocess — the L1 completeness gate.

  Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other
  BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it
  by `bun run render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.

  The <folio:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill
  that implements it; <folio:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared
  work plan in beans/.
-->
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:folio="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/bpmn"
                  id="Definitions_L1Gate"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_L1Gate">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_L1Gate" name="Ingestion subprocess — the L1 completeness gate" processRef="Process_L1Gate" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L1Gate" name="Ingestion subprocess — the L1 completeness gate" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>folio-assistant — Ingestion subprocess — the L1 completeness gate.

  Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other
  BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it
  by `bun run render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.

  The &lt;folio:skill&gt; extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill
  that implements it; &lt;folio:bean&gt; marks a step that reads or writes the shared
  work plan in beans/.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <folio:policy enforcement="advisory" />
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="Process_L1Gate_LaneSet">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_0" name="Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Runs both QA checks unattended and hands off exactly where the role's persona says it must: Gateway_Drift's 'drift' branch leaves this lane the moment a passage needs a judgement about which of two readings is right, rather than guessing — but Task_Verdict, which records the outcome either way, stays in this lane, so Lane_1 adjudicates a single passage while this lane still owns the completeness verdict as a whole.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>StartEvent_KgBuilt</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_CheckDerived</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RoundTrip</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Drift</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Verdict</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_Verdict</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_1" name="Reviewer (SME or editor)">
        <bpmn:documentation>The only human involvement anywhere in this subprocess: Lane_0 runs both checks and records the verdict unattended, so this lane exists solely for the single case machine QA cannot resolve on its own — a flagged passage where round-trip translation produced two different readings and somebody has to say which is right.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_FlagDrift</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_KgBuilt" name="L1 graph built">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_g1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_CheckDerived" name="Is every derived
artefact present?">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="document-intake"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>

      <bpmn:documentation>L1 source to L1 KG is NOT complete while a required derived artefact is missing. This is the gate that makes the derivation steps obligatory rather than aspirational.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_g1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_g2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_RoundTrip" name="Round-trip translation QA">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="document-intake"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>

      <bpmn:documentation>NOT IMPLEMENTED. Tracked as a bean; see docs/document-ingestion.md. Back-translate each localized narrative into its source language and compare meaning, to catch semantic drift and bad terminology that a forward-only check cannot see.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_g2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_g3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Drift" name="Drift or bad
terminology?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Answered by the round-trip translation QA: did it flag semantic drift or a terminology miss? `drift` sends the passage to a person to adjudicate, since which reading is right is a human call; `clean` records the verdict directly.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_g3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_g4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_g6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_FlagDrift" calledElement="Process_Adjudication" name="Adjudicate the
flagged passage">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="document-intake"/>
        <folio:skill ref="adjudication"/>
        <folio:adjudication codes="drift false-positive"/>
        <folio:fulfilment kinds="person agent" reason="the restriction Process_Adjudication states on A_Adjudicate, restated here because this is where the enum is declared; the engine refuses system or external on any step carrying folio:adjudication."/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>

      <bpmn:documentation>A machine can detect that two readings differ. Which one is right is a human call.

Permitted answers (bean `bvuk`, owner 2026-09-23): `drift` — the translation lost or changed the meaning; `false-positive` — the two readings say the same thing. Task_Verdict records either; nothing branches here.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_g4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_g5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Verdict" name="Record the L1
completeness verdict">
      <bpmn:documentation>Record the completeness verdict in three states — met, unmet, or not yet derivable — as bun run check:l1-complete reports it. Not-yet-derivable is never a pass. An unmet verdict opens a bean and returns to derivation; only a met one lets the entry into library/.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <folio:skill ref="document-intake"/>
        <folio:bean op="note" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_g5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_g6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_g7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_Verdict" name="Verdict recorded">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_g7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_g1" sourceRef="StartEvent_KgBuilt" targetRef="Task_CheckDerived" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_g2" sourceRef="Task_CheckDerived" targetRef="Task_RoundTrip" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_g3" sourceRef="Task_RoundTrip" targetRef="Gateway_Drift" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_g4" name="drift" sourceRef="Gateway_Drift" targetRef="Task_FlagDrift" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_g5" sourceRef="Task_FlagDrift" targetRef="Task_Verdict" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_g6" name="clean" sourceRef="Gateway_Drift" targetRef="Task_Verdict" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_g7" sourceRef="Task_Verdict" targetRef="EndEvent_Verdict" />
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L1Gate">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L1Gate" bpmnElement="Collaboration_L1Gate">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Participant_L1Gate_di" bpmnElement="Participant_L1Gate" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1450" height="360" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_0_di" bpmnElement="Lane_0" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="190" y="80" width="1420" height="180" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_1_di" bpmnElement="Lane_1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="190" y="260" width="1420" height="180" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_KgBuilt_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_KgBuilt"><dc:Bounds x="277" y="152" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_CheckDerived_di" bpmnElement="Task_CheckDerived"><dc:Bounds x="410" y="130" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_RoundTrip_di" bpmnElement="Task_RoundTrip"><dc:Bounds x="600" y="130" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Drift_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Drift"><dc:Bounds x="840" y="145" width="50" height="50" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_FlagDrift_di" bpmnElement="Task_FlagDrift"><dc:Bounds x="980" y="310" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Verdict_di" bpmnElement="Task_Verdict"><dc:Bounds x="1170" y="130" width="150" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_Verdict_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_Verdict"><dc:Bounds x="1417" y="152" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_g1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_g1"><di:waypoint x="313" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="410" y="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_g2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_g2"><di:waypoint x="560" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="600" y="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_g3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_g3"><di:waypoint x="750" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="840" y="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_g4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_g4"><di:waypoint x="890" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="950" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="950" y="350" /><di:waypoint x="980" y="350" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_g5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_g5"><di:waypoint x="1130" y="350" /><di:waypoint x="1140" y="350" /><di:waypoint x="1140" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="1170" y="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_g6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_g6"><di:waypoint x="890" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="1170" y="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_g7_di" bpmnElement="Flow_g7"><di:waypoint x="1320" y="170" /><di:waypoint x="1417" y="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
